MARKETING WORKFLOW
→ 658.8 → Marketing
organize files → connect references → give agents what they need

WORKFLOW
  task (e.g. launch page + social posts)
    → agent reads brief + customer + offer + voice + proof + performance
    → agent reads brand book + visual refs
    → create + self-check
    → you review claims / offer / voice / design / links
    → revise from feedback
    → after sign-off: publish → collect results
    → save back: edits to voice.md / examples / warehouse / moodboard

RULES
  markdown in GitHub (reviewable, traceable)
  large creative files linked from shared storage
  start with one function and one task you already do
  update sources from real work: corrections, new objections, offer changes

SHARED CORE  (.md)
  company.md       what the business does and who it serves
  customer.md      problems, buying triggers, objections, customer language
  offer.md         what you sell, pricing, deliverables, supportable promises
  positioning.md   why choose you over alternatives
  voice.md         how you write + examples + phrases to avoid + your edits
  proof.md         case studies, approved claims, evidence links
  AGENTS.md        where to read / save / flag conflicts / ask for sign-off

FUNCTION FOLDERS
  content/   seo/   paid/   creator/   email/
    playbook.md    how the work gets done
    examples/      approved work + rejected versions + your feedback
    tools.md       tools and accounts agents can use
    checks.md      what to verify before returning work
    calendar.md    planned / in progress / ready for review

PLATFORM FOLDERS  (inside content/)
  x/   linkedin/   newsletter/   visual/
    formats you use
    approved examples
    rejected drafts + why

VISUAL REFERENCES
  moodboard        look references + notes on what you like
  brand book       colors, fonts, logos, layouts, usage rules
  approved assets  previous ads, landing pages, campaign visuals
  (Figma or Paper — link from visual/)

CAMPAIGN FOLDER
  campaigns/product-launch/
    brief.md       goal, audience, offer, constraints
    research/
    decisions.md   what was agreed and why (rejected angles, offer changes)
    production/
    results.md     performance + interpretation

DATA WAREHOUSE
  connect ads, analytics, sales, content accounts
  store spend, clicks, leads, conversions, campaign results
  agents query previous performance by campaign / asset / date
  include reporting period + metric definitions


